okay let's talk today about Iran  Venezuela and Syria and I mentioned  yesterday that I want to discuss the  Putin angle on the latest Iran stuff but  I also want to talk about it in the  larger context and there's a really good  post about this on our subreddit david  pakman.com slash reddit which outlines  sort of the underlying idea that i want  to present to you here and it's  something i've been thinking about i  thought about it over the weekend as the  iran news was breaking and i've  continued thinking about it and the idea  is that in the end donald trump may be  destined to stay out of iran and stay  out of venezuela and ultimately stay out  of syria in any serious way because  staying out of those three countries  shares a common thread which is that  it's in vladimir putin's and russia's  interests for the united states to stay  out of those three countries now III  know I know that I have to issue this  disclaimer I hope we can be mature here  okay this is not Putin is literally  telling Trump what to do although who  knows what they've talked about in  private we actually don't know but it's  the trend once again that in the end  when the rubber meets the road  Trump ends up taking the path that is in  Russia's interests and this is not about  collusion or Trump criminality or  anything like that  it's about geopolitical realities it's  about the realities of the dynamics that  are forming as I've talked to you about  many times now among the three major  superpowers right now the United States  China and Russia in a way that is not  very good for the United States under  Donald Trump Iran Venezuela and Syria  are three allies of Russia and the trend  in Donald Trump's presidency it's not a  hundred percent but it's a high  percentage is that in the end rhetoric  aside Trump ends up acting in a way that  protects or doesn't go against or  threaten Russia's interests and let's go  through them one by one here Trump does  a big boy and he attacks Syria except he  attacked an empty runway at an airport  after telling Russia that he was going  to do it and it was back up and running  within a couple of days if not more like  hours and so for all of the tough talk  Trump does effectively nothing now this  doesn't mean I want Trump intervening in  Syria what we're doing here is an  analysis of how Trump's actions relate  to Russia's interests not me saying I  want Trump to take a B or C action  that's Syria Venezuela number two in the  winter as I told you last week Donald  Trump was looking very hard at going  into Venezuela forcing regime change to  be clear I don't want him to do that  I'm glad that Donald Trump didn't do  that don't email me saying I want Trump  to intervene in Venezuela because I  don't but last week I told you that  there are some new reports from inside  sources would say that Donald Trump  simply got bored and sort of lost  patience with the complexity of the  entire Venezuela thing which is totally  believable but once again in the end it  favors Vladimir Putin Putin and the  shabbos Maduro regime are tight we know  that much of the change in Donald  Trump's focus on Venezuela happened  after a phone call with Vladimir Putin  in early May and once again in the end  Donald Trump takes the path that at  least in the immediate is the one that  protects Russia's interests and favors  favors Vladimir Putin and then number  three we now have Iran yes the bluster  against Iran the threats the sanctions  and threats of sanctions backing out of  the Iran deal the entire thing we told  you about yesterday including Donald  Trump authorizing a strike against Iran  over the weekend but then calling it off  says it was over civilian casualty  estimates which may be true but once  again Trump despite the domineering  rhetoric ends up taking the action or  more accurately not taking the action  that favors Vladimir Putin and is in  Russia's interests so again please don't  make this out to be me saying anything  other than what I'm actually saying I am  NOT saying Trump is personally colluding  with Putin on these three foreign policy  situations  I'm not alleging to alleging or pointing  to some kind of conspiracy I'm pointing  out that in the end Donald Trump is  taking the paths here that Putin would  want him to take if you're concerned  with what's in the United States best  interests then you have to be concerned  about the u.s. increasingly being in a  position relative to the two to the two  other major superpowers Russia and China  who as I've told you before are  increasingly working together at the  disadvantage of and exclusion of the  United States now maybe you don't care  about that I mean there are people who  even though they might live in the  United States as most but not all of our  audience does who don't care if the  United States is better or worse  position than they say we're all humans  I don't care about country borders and I  don't care as long as we raise the  overall well-being that's my concern I  don't care what happens to the United  States many of us even on the Left who  live in the United States are invested  in the United States being a good place  to live in a place that has a good  standard of living and the relationships  we would like to see with other  countries and so we do care about this  so please don't start with the you know  I must be a war monger stuff because I'm  criticizing Trump for not going into  Iran Syria or Venezuela I want Bashar al  Assad out for the sake of the Syrian  people but not at the hands of the  United States I think the United States  needs to stay totally out of Venezuela I  do not want Donald Trump starting a war  with Iran this is not about me  personally these erratic maneuvers by  Trump are odd baiting Iran into action  pulling the u.s. out of the Iran deal  getting the opportunity to keep  escalating and then now last-minute  bailing on the escalation if a  Democratic president had done this it  would be every low-rent right-wing  analyst on Fox News 24/7 talking about  how weak Obama or Hillary or whoever was  by virtue of taking the action that  Donald Trump has taken so my concern is  the underlying geopolitical concerns  that exist here and number two whether  Donald Trump is actually in the end  making the decisions that even he  believes are in the best interests of  the United States I know that I wouldn't  agree with his conclusions about what's  best for the United States but at least  I would like to believe that in good  faith that's what his decisions are  informed by even if I would disagree  with the conclusions it's not clear that  that's going on based on how at least  these three situations are playing out  in the end let me know you're thinking  about this and play a few  gonna do the conspiratorial you know  allegations  don't even bother I'm not going to  respond I'm not going to engage but if  you have a serious thought about what  I've laid out here I actually do want to  hear from you

